{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1045","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1045","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1045\",\"parent_revision\":\"7b45a78a61b076ae1aecffcf74df93f480050d9cf15e8a44ec72d0a551433f86\",\"root_revision\":\"7b45a78a61b076ae1aecffcf74df93f480050d9cf15e8a44ec72d0a551433f86\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nsam_ready was called 10x with identical input {\\\"plan\\\":\\\"P036\\\"} in session d9625523 (records 263,276,288,300,335,346,388,442,451,470). Each call returns ~4,236 chars avg. The dispatch loop re-fetches ready tasks on every iteration instead of calling once and looping over the result. Fix: add explicit instruction to skill \u2014 call sam_ready once per dispatch cycle, store the result, loop over it without re-calling. Use sam_status (270 chars avg) as the loop-continuation check instead.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Session waste compounds across every implement-feature run; each redundant sam_ready call adds ~4,236 chars of unnecessary context, multiplied by 10 calls per session = ~42K chars wasted per session.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Bottleneck: every implement-feature session accumulates ~42K chars of unnecessary context from sam_ready re-calls, reducing available context window for actual task work\\n- Blocks: sessions on large plans may hit context limits prematurely\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates ~42K chars of redundant context consumption per implement-feature session\\n- Replaces sam_ready loop re-calls with sam_status (~270 chars) for continuation checks\\n- Instruction change is low-risk and immediately effective\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nsam_ready (or backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks) is called once per dispatch batch. The returned task list is stored and iterated. After all tasks in the batch complete, sam_status is called to determine whether another batch is needed. sam_ready is only called again when a new batch is required.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe implement-feature SKILL.md Progress Loop section contains an unambiguous call-once instruction that:\\n1. Prohibits calling sam_ready inside the per-task loop\\n2. Specifies sam_status (~270 chars) as the loop-continuation check\\n3. Specifies sam_ready only when a new batch is needed after the previous batch is fully dispatched\\n\\nThe dispatch SKILL.md manager pattern either references this rule or contains its own fetch-once instruction (the dispatch skill already contains a fetch-once rule for backlog_view; sam_ready should receive equivalent treatment).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. implement-feature SKILL.md contains an explicit instruction: call sam_ready once per batch, store the result, loop over stored list \u2014 do NOT call sam_ready again within the loop\\n2. The instruction specifies sam_status as the loop-continuation check between batches\\n3. The instruction is positioned immediately before or within the step that calls sam_ready (not buried in a later note)\\n4. A session replay of a multi-task plan produces exactly one sam_ready call per batch of ready tasks (verifiable via session tool-call log)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature \u2014 Progress Loop section, lines 44\u201365 (call-once instruction already present here) |\\n| Skill | /dh:dispatch \u2014 Section 1 \\\"Set Up the Team\\\" already has fetch-once rule for backlog_view (lines 37\u201338); sam_ready should get equivalent treatment |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the call-once instruction already exists in implement-feature SKILL.md at lines 60\u201365. Work is: (1) verify the instruction is correctly positioned and unambiguous, (2) optionally add a parallel fetch-once note for sam_ready in dispatch SKILL.md. Pure documentation/instruction edit, no code change needed.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **implement-feature/dispatch skill: sam_ready called 10x identically per session \u2014 add call-once instruction** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: vm-flightsimulator session waste audit 2026-03-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"75899ac9c9ec6f3f15a437ab122136cc45b3849f4b6213d5c0418be87353cd01\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS7qJQ\"}"}